<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-natural-numbers" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Natural Numbers</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      How many students are in your class? How many days are in a year? How many cards are in a deck?
    </p>
    <p>
      Humans invented numbers to count, organise, compare, and describe the world around them.
      Natural numbers are the counting numbers: 1, 2, 3, 4, ...
    </p>
    <p>
      In this chapter we investigate natural numbers, their patterns, operations, and properties.
      We explore how to represent numbers in different ways, how operations work, and why certain properties matter.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="num_counting.ptx" />
